<page-header title="pstack Playbooks">
  <@lede>Every playbook in poteto's pstack, one lane each, plus the entry that picks one and the fallback skill.</@lede>
  <@how>Each playbook is one lane, read left to right. Point at a step or a labelled connector and its details open in the panel on the right. Click to pin them; click again to release. <Kbd>Esc</Kbd> closes the panel. The address of the page records a pinned selection, so a link to it shares it. A step with no icon is done from the playbook's own text.</@how>
  <@meta>Drawn 2026-11-17 from cursor/plugins @2f87c85, pstack/skills/poteto-mode. SKILL.md, worker.md, figure-it-out and all 22 playbooks were read in full by the lead; watch-pr, worktree-audit.sh, log.sh and bootstrap.ts in full by subagents (notes/research/agent-stacks/pstack/scripts/). Nothing was run. Dotted connectors are our inference, not the playbook's words.</@meta>
</page-header>

